          up: {"title":"Match the language (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Eight languages of the wider region, with closely worded descriptions. Read each one carefully.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Garifuna","r":"Arawakan language of a people exiled from St Vincent, now spoken in Belize and Central America"},{"l":"Lokono","r":"Arawakan indigenous language of the Guiana coast"},{"l":"Q'eqchi'","r":"Mayan language spoken in southern Belize"},{"l":"Sarnami","r":"Suriname's variety of Hindustani, developed mainly from the Bhojpuri of indentured labourers"},{"l":"Javanese","r":"Asian language brought to Suriname by indentured workers from Indonesia"},{"l":"Belize Kriol","r":"English-lexified creole used as the lingua franca of Belize"},{"l":"Trinidad French Creole","r":"Endangered French-lexified creole spoken mainly by older people"},{"l":"Saramaccan","r":"Maroon creole of Suriname's interior with many Portuguese-derived words"}],"win":"Excellent. You distinguished indigenous, Asian and creole languages and noticed details of origin, status and vitality."}
